From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] [CUDA] Support round-to-nearest-even TF32 casts

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Upstream-commit: c99577fd910538b7cc24136fb943a04008261be3

Rationale: Lower T.cast(x, T.tfloat32) had only emitted bitwise truncation (cvt.rna.tf32.f32 / & 0xFFFFE000), preventing 2-split round-to-nearest-even TF32 decomposition where a signed remainder captures full 24-bit FP32 precision in two tensor-core GEMMs instead of three. Add optional round="rn"|"rz" mode to T.cast/T.Cast for TF32 casts, lowering round="rn" to tl::cast_rn_tf32 (cvt.rn.tf32.f32 on SM80+).

Quality: Preserves existing truncation behavior by default; round="rn" is opt-in and reduces mHC project_streams 2-split relative error against FP64 below 3-split truncation (2.1e-6..3.1e-6 vs 2.5e-6..3.7e-6).

Tests: testing/python/language/test_tilelang_language_cast.py (test_tf32_cast_round_modes) and mHC 2-split parity checks across two GPU boots on SM121.

Upstream-status: Backported from tile-ai/tilelang#3714 (commit c99577fd910538b7cc24136fb943a04008261be3).
